PAIS FIELD DRIVE vs MHD
TABLETOP PAIS-EFFECT TEST
Source: @BlokeMan00

This is a low-energy measurement model, not a recreation of
the patent’s extreme fields. It only asks whether any
repeatable anomaly exists at laboratory scale.
Independent vacuum replication would be required before
any claim of new physics.

CONCEPT
Pais-style field drive claims to change a vehicle’s effective inertia
with intense, high-frequency electromagnetic fields.
No plasma exhaust. No onboard propellant. Effectively unlimited Isp.

MHD propulsion ionizes a conductive fluid and accelerates it with
B and E fields. Requires tanks, high power, electrode wear, heat
management. Thrust is limited by mass flow.

CLAIMED ADVANTAGE
Alter inertial mass instead of throwing reaction mass.
Potential for high acceleration without a plume.

APPARATUS (TABLETOP MODEL)
Type: torsion / flexure force sensor
Test body: lightweight nonmagnetic disk or rotor
Suspension: torsion fiber or flexure mount
Sensing: laser + optical lever / position sensor
Fields: opposing EM coils (time-varying B)
        capacitor plates or resonant electrodes (time-varying E)
Drive: function generator + amplifier
Isolation: Faraday cage, vacuum preferred, nonmagnetic frame
Monitors: temperature, power, polarity, phase

CORE QUESTION
Does a rapidly changing EM field produce anomalous force
or a change in inertia that standard EM cannot explain?

KEY VARIABLES
F_app     measured force or torque on the disk
P_elec    applied electrical power
B(t)      alternating magnetic field
E(t)      alternating electric field
phi       relative phase between E and B
f         frequency (kHz–MHz range in lab model)
m_eff     claimed effective inertial mass
Isp       specific impulse (claimed unlimited for field drive)

FIGURE OF MERIT
F_app / P_elec   (N/W)

If this ratio stays after all artifact controls and does not
scale like ordinary magnetic, electrostatic, thermal, or
radiation-pressure forces, the result is anomalous.

STAGED PROTOCOL
Baseline          power off, record drift and noise
Magnetic-only     coils on, electrodes off
Electric-only     electrodes on, coils off
Combined-field    E + B with adjustable phase
Reversal          flip coil polarity and electrode orientation
Dummy-load        electronics on, field elements disconnected
Blind             randomized on/off by a second operator

A real effect should reverse or change predictably with
geometry and phase, survive vacuum, and survive dummy-load.

FALSE-SIGNAL SOURCES
air currents, fan vibration, transformer hum,
wire reaction forces, magnetic attraction to hardware,
electrostatic pull, heating / expansion, corona,
Earth’s magnetic field, acoustic pressure

FUNDAMENTALS
Inertia          resistance to acceleration (m in F = ma)
MHD              magnetohydrodynamics — force on current in B field
Pais Effect      patented claim that high-frequency EM fields
                 interact with vacuum fluctuations to reduce
                 inertial mass (Navy patents ~2016–2019;
                 no public confirmation at spacecraft scale)
Torsion sensor   converts tiny torque into measurable angle
Optical lever    amplifies microscopic displacement

